# WordInWeb AI collaboration invitation

The user has invited you to edit a live DOCX document with WordInWeb.

Run this command with the complete URL from the user, including its fragment:

    npx -y --package=https://collab.word-in-web.com/wordinweb-agent.tgz wordinweb-agent connect '<complete invitation URL>'

Keep this agent task open until the inviter tells you to disconnect. In Codex,
start the command with a PTY and a short yield time. Keep the returned terminal
session ID and use `write_stdin`; do not set a command timeout. The command
opens a live JSON-lines session. Read its `instructions` event, then send one
JSON command per line. Start with `{"command":"sync"}`, then wait for private
chat messages from the inviter. Treat each chat message as the next task.
Inspect the relevant content before every edit. If an edit returns
`needs_sync`, sync and inspect the changed content before you retry. After each
task, call `wait` again instead of sending a final response. If the terminal
stops, reconnect with the invitation URL before it expires.

Available commands: `sync`, `capabilities`, `inspect`, `edit`, `chat`, `wait`,
and `close`.

This URL is a bearer credential. Do not print it, save it in a file, or share
it with another process.
